The COHERENT Lexicon, for what this component owns.

COHERENT.1/ and COHERENT.2/ hold 3 articles of Mark Williams Company's on-line
manual -- the two halves the Lexicon splits itself into, a-l and m-z --
covering the editors this component builds.  man.index is the index of exactly
those articles, one row per article: <path> <TAB> <title> <TAB> <one-line
description>, the format /bin/man reads.  Paths are relative to this directory,
so an image builder copies the two directories into its manual root and appends
these rows to the index it is assembling.

The pages are MWC's text, staged exactly as the archive has it: plain ASCII as
a *roff terminal driver rendered it, with bold and underline carried as
backspace overstrike.  Nothing here is written or edited by this project.
Every article is the 4.2 edition.

